# Selah Flutter

Feature-first layers: `presentation` → Riverpod `application` → `domain` → `data`.

- Domain is pure Dart. No Flutter or Drift imports.
- Entities are plain immutable classes. Do not add freezed.
- The journal is offline by default. Optional email sign-in and group sync to `SELAH_API_BASE_URL` are the only network path; Just me prayers never leave the device. Do not add analytics or other background network.
- Display name comes from `AppConfig.appName`.
- New Drift tables or columns: edit `lib/core/db/tables.dart`, run `dart run build_runner build`, commit the generated `.g.dart`.
- Verse rows are added in `tool/generate_verses.py`, then `python3 tool/generate_verses.py` and `dart run tool/build_verses.dart`. Do not hand-write KJV text into JSON.
- Prayer strategies in `assets/verses/strategies.json` only choose verses (`triggers`, `seedRefs`, `alwaysOn`, `order`). They are not shown in the UI.
- Keep tap targets at least 48px, label icon-only buttons, and avoid overflow at 200% text scale.
- Cover suggester and repository changes with tests under `test/`.

```dart
// Bad: domain imports Flutter
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

// Good: domain stays pure Dart
class Prayer { const Prayer({required this.id}); final int id; }
```
